.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-dns-acme-key-create - Create an ACME key


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro dns acme-key create  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create an ACME key

.PP
A key for certificate automation that can only add/remove \fB_acme-challenge\fR TXT records (scope \fBdns_acme\fR), optionally only in \fBzones\fR and only from \fBips\fR\&. It cannot read zones, change other records or reach any other endpoint. The token is returned once. Max 10 per service.

.PP
API: POST /cloud/dns/{id}/acme-keys (operationId createAcmeKey, scope services_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--data\fP=""
	request body as JSON, @file or @- (stdin)

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	idempotency key (automatic for money operations)

.PP
\fB--ips\fP=[]
	Allowed client IPs (empty = any)

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	Label (e.g. web-01)

.PP
\fB--set\fP=[]
	extra body field key=value (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--zones\fP=[]
	Allowed zones (empty = all zones of the service)


